With great thanks to LeanEuclid
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Our tacit rules (Elements/Foundations/Tacit/) follow the System E of Jeremy
Avigad, Edward Dean and John Mumma ("A formal system for Euclid's Elements",
Review of Symbolic Logic 2(4), 2009). While writing them we kept LeanEuclid's
Lean rendering of System E open beside the paper the whole time, and we owe
it a great deal:

  * our single superposition rule follows LeanEuclid's combined form of
    System E's two superposition rules;
  * our Intersection rule 4 (circles_meet_of_on_inside_outside) uses
    LeanEuclid's corrected hypothesis ("on the circle"), which fixes a
    statement in the published paper that fails for a small circle lying
    inside a larger one;
  * our reading of the Points construction rules and the transfer rules was
    checked against theirs line by line.

LeanEuclid: https://github.com/loganrjmurphy/LeanEuclid
by Logan Murphy, Kaiyu Yang, Jialiang Sun, Zhaoyu Li, Anima Anandkumar and
Xujie Si ("Autoformalizing Euclidean Geometry", ICML 2024). Thank you all!
